# Playing the first release, from orbit to a second territory.
#
# `releases/first-release.md` gives the loop in eight steps. This file walks the first five:
# no presence on the planet, land the ark and claim a territory, work the food extractor to
# grow the population, build extractors for metal and energy, then produce a pioneer and
# spread across the planet by land.
#
# Every line is a command. There is no other way for the state to move, so this file is a
# complete account of the game it produces.

# 1 and 2. The ark comes down, and landing *is* the claiming: it takes the ground and
# becomes a garrison to hold it, a citizen, and one extractor for each resource.
#
# Three extractors rather than one, because `P-152` conserves metal and an extractor costs
# some. A landing site that arrived with only a farm could never afford its first mine.
land ark 1

# Turn 1. One citizen, one hand, and the farm is the only thing worth spending it on.
work 1 extractor 1 food
end turn

# Turn 2. Two citizens. One holds the food, one opens the mine - and the metal must be spent
# this turn, because a store does not survive the end of one.
work 1 extractor 1 food
work 1 extractor 1 metal
end turn

# Turn 3. Four citizens. Every extractor the landing left is worked, and the spare hand and the
# spare metal become a second farm.
work 1 extractor 1 food
work 1 extractor 1 metal
work 1 extractor 1 energy
build extractor 1 food
end turn

# Turn 4. Two farms feed eight, which is the first turn the population is limited by hands
# rather than by food.
work 2 extractor 1 food
work 1 extractor 1 metal
work 1 extractor 1 energy
end turn

# Turn 5. Eight citizens, and four spare hands with four metal to spend: the third farm, two
# more mines, a second well.
work 2 extractor 1 food
work 1 extractor 1 metal
work 1 extractor 1 energy
build extractor 1 food
build extractor 1 metal
build extractor 1 metal
build extractor 1 energy
end turn

# Turn 6. Everything is worked. Twelve food feeds twelve, and the population settles there.
work 3 extractor 1 food
work 3 extractor 1 metal
work 2 extractor 1 energy
end turn

# Turn 7. The last well. From here the territory is complete: three farms, three mines, three
# wells, and twelve of each a turn.
work 3 extractor 1 food
work 3 extractor 1 metal
work 2 extractor 1 energy
build extractor 1 energy
end turn

# Turn 8. Twelve metal and twelve energy against a pioneer's two and six.
work 3 extractor 1 food
work 3 extractor 1 metal
work 3 extractor 1 energy

# 5. The landing site can send a pioneer out.
produce pioneer 1
end turn

# Turn 9. The farms are worked first - a population that gathers nothing this turn starves
# at the end of it, whatever else is going on.
work 3 extractor 1 food
work 3 extractor 1 metal
work 3 extractor 1 energy

# The pioneer crosses into a neighbouring territory. It is not held, so arriving there takes
# it and claims it: force 2 against a force of nature of 1, and the pioneer becomes the
# garrison, citizen and food extractor the new ground needs.
move pioneer 2

# The new territory arrives with a citizen and a farm, both ready, so it feeds itself on the
# very turn it is claimed.
work 1 extractor 2 food
end turn
